This repository contains two kinds of material, licensed differently.

================================================================================
1. CODE AND ORIGINAL WRITING: MIT Licence
================================================================================

Applies to: everything in this repository EXCEPT two things, both of which live in
data/ and are covered by clause 2 below. Those two are the figures themselves, and
the passages quoted from the publications the figures came from.

So this clause covers the site's own prose in content/, the build code in lib/,
scripts/ and eleventy.config.js, the documentation in docs/, README.md,
CHANGELOG.md, the workflows in .github/, and the writing carried in the data files
themselves: the card paragraphs, notes and caveats are this project's words, not
the publishers'.

The scope is written this way round on purpose. It was an enumeration, and an
enumeration is a list of what someone remembered: it named scripts/, README.md
and docs/, so every word of the pages a reader actually reads was licensed by
neither clause. A reuser should not have to guess, and a citing outlet's legal
desk will not.

